From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ts4-port <ts4-port@localhost>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:06:15 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 27/35] android: load a custom Vulkan driver via libadrenotools
 (nfsmw sdk)

Vendors libadrenotools + linkernsbypass (BSD-2) from codepdbh/nfsmw-android's
sdk/thirdparty, plus its 21-line android_gpu_driver wrapper, and routes the
Android Vulkan loader through it. The driver is selected by environment
variables (REX_NATIVE_LIB_DIR, REX_GPU_DRIVER_DIR/NAME/TMP) because the app
sets them before the native library loads; with none set the wrapper falls
back to dlopen("libvulkan.so") exactly as before.

Why: Mesa Turnip reports shaderInt64 = true (src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc)
while the Qualcomm blob reports false, so the port's native renderer gate only
opens on Turnip. Verified on device: MesaTurnip/PurpleVK 26.3, shaderInt64
present, native renderer enabled.
